1
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,460
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,060
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,260
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,340
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,820
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,100
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:06,340
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:08,380
(Wang Churan)

9
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:10,420
(Lin Yi)

10
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:15,860
=Natural High S4=

11
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:35,700
=EP4 (Part 1): A Fun Trip to Songpan=

12
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:38,720
Time to eat.

13
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:41,180
Bai, are we friends despite the age gap?

14
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:42,400
You're pretty old already, Bai.

15
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,040
We're

16
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:44,760
ten years apart.

17
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:46,640
What?

18
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,040
Ten years?

19
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,600
Weren't you born in 1990 or 1991?

20
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:50,800
I was born in 1993.

21
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:52,560
Seven years.

22
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,360
That's almost ten.

23
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,960
(Only Bai gets roasted)
♪Sometimes talking to people♪

24
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:59,680
♪Just doesn't work♪

25
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,080
(Why'd you get him started?)
Alright.

26
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:13,420
(Petting the cat)

27
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,820
(A little tantrum)

28
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,080
Everyone,

29
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,640
today, we have

30
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,840
a special guest.

31
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:25,280
He once gave us

32
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,360
(Wang Anyu)
one of the most iconic moments

33
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,200
in Werewolf history.
Two wolves recognizing each other.

34
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,840
Don't tell me it's Lin Yi.

35
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:34,640
Let's give Lin Yi a big hand!

36
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,680
Hey, everyone.

37
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:38,440
Hello.

38
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:39,240
Long time no see.

39
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:40,680
Teng.

40
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:44,180
(Another missed high five)

41
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:45,600
(Totally clueless)
This is my seat, right?

42
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:47,640
I wanted a high five.

43
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,440
Teng.

44
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,160
Hey.

45
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:51,760
Hello.

46
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,600
I even put in contacts for this.

47
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,880
(Lesson learned)
Two special cards.

48
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,160
Open your eyes.

49
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:56,960
Today, I'm gonna

50
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,480
keep my eyes peeled.

51
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,600
When Teng heard you were coming,

52
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,880
(Hu Xianxu)
he begged the crew overnight

53
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,400
to scrap every Werewolf game.

54
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,520
Today, we're
having traditional Zang cuisine.

55
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,820
(Cold yak salad)

56
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:10,940
(Stir-fried yak with pickled greens)

57
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:12,100
(Yak sausage)

58
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,460
(Yak sashimi)
Oh my God.

59
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:14,320
(Zang-style pickled greens noodles,
blanket-covered yak)

60
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,600
(Hand-eaten yak meat)
Smells amazing.

61
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:17,180
(Zang-style steamed buns,
highland yak tongue)

62
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:18,500
(Matsutake yak fried rice,
free-range chicken and matsutake soup)

63
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:22,960
Did our team

64
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:24,600
really do that badly?

65
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,600
It's all cold dishes.

66
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,760
These are cold too?

67
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:29,760
- Where's the hot food?
- What's this?

68
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,880
Cold dish.

69
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,320
Cold too?

70
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,520
Oh, that's fine then.

71
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,460
(Never mind then)

72
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:37,800
Thanks, Hu.

73
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:41,960
No bowls left?

74
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,580
(Hu's missing bowl 2.0)

75
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,000
I'll go find one.

76
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,180
(Constant eye contact)

77
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:48,760
So fresh.

78
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,040
Quick, while it's hot.

79
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,000
You eat this raw?

80
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,320
You dip it in this, right?

81
00:03:59,320 --> 00:03:59,920
Wasabi.

82
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,480
It's so good.

83
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,120
The texture's really unique.

84
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,080
And it's super tender.

85
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,280
Didn't we have this in Nyingchi

86
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:04,960
last time?

87
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:06,280
Yeah, in Nyingchi.

88
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,440
Yeah. I forgot where.

89
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,240
I've had this before.

90
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:10,260
(Giving it a try)

91
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,260
(Wasabi)

92
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,200
Didn't mix it well.

93
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,220
(Such a helpful northeastern kid)
The wasabi wasn't mixed well.

94
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:23,680
It's my second time having this.
It's great.

95
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,940
(That wasabi packs a punch)

96
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:34,980
(Wasabi)

97
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:36,720
Let me try.

98
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,380
(Just a little taste)

99
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,660
(Savoring it)

100
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:41,580
(Mmm, not bad)

101
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:42,540
(Wait, no)

102
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:49,180
(Wasabi)

103
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:49,960
Too much wasabi.

104
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Have some soup.

105
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,800
I got a huge mouthful of wasabi.

106
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:03,860
(Wasabi)

107
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:04,980
(Nobody's safe from the wasabi)

108
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:05,640
Bing.

109
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:06,280
Bing's eating and...

110
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:09,680
His eyes are already red.

111
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,920
Quick, get a close-up.

112
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,240
(Jia Bing)
I pick Bing.

113
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,120
I wanna see...

114
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,080
Yesterday's top two.

115
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,400
Those teary eyes melt our hearts.

116
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,600
Because he wanted to see them.

117
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:24,180
(He got his wish)

118
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,560
Lin Yi, dig in.

119
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,200
Grab your chopsticks.

120
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:32,920
I am.

121
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,680
This sashimi's amazing.

122
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:35,800
Try something else too.

123
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,040
I'll eat as I go.

124
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:39,600
Go table-hopping.

125
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:41,020
(A little too welcoming)

126
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,160
Just kidding.

127
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,680
If you like it, have some more of it.

128
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:48,160
You practically traumatized Lin Yi.

129
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,680
His eyes were so wide.

130
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,280
Wider than ever since he got here.

131
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:57,360
No.

132
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,760
I've been keeping Teng
in the corner of my eye.

133
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,160
Can't risk missing a single glance.

134
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:05,020
(Always on alert)

135
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:05,880
Nice.

136
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,280
Lin Yi, you
were born in the 2000s, right?

137
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:11,440
Actually, 1999.

138
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,760
Just one year off.

139
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,240
Churan, you were born
in the 2000s, right?

140
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:17,720
1999 too.

141
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,320
You're a '99 baby too?

142
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:19,200
What month?

143
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:19,840
January.

144
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:20,600
Me too.

145
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:22,720
Which day?

146
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,720
Sometime after the 20th of January.

147
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:24,880
(January 11, 1999, January 21, 1999)

148
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:25,360
Little sis.

149
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:26,880
Little sis.

150
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,680
I'm January 11.

151
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,600
January 21 for me.

152
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,360
You're only ten days apart.

153
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,400
Then we're not the same zodiac sign.

154
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,000
You're a Capricorn. I'm an Aquarius.

155
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,600
(Huang Jingyu)
You two should keep digging.

156
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,880
Maybe you're from the same hometown.

157
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,240
What, you two falling
for each other already?

158
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,000
Were you even born in the same hospital?

159
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,760
By the time they're done,
all the cold dishes will be gone.

160
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:48,860
(Wang Churan)

161
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,360
How many days have you been filming?

162
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,000
Day three.

163
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:55,520
Were the meals pretty basic
the first few days?

164
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,680
No, Bing cooked everything.

165
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:58,800
So, have you had that...

166
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,640
Xu Fu risotto yet?

167
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,280
Yeah, but Teng didn't make it.

168
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,760
Lin Yi, eat up.

169
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,600
I am, Teng.

170
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:08,580
(Xu Fu's too busy stuffing his face)

171
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,040
Today,

172
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:17,560
we've got a singing challenge.

173
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,080
Anyu was just eating,

174
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:20,780
then suddenly perked right up.

175
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:21,240
The second he heard that,

176
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,440
(His specialty)
he already knew what he'd sing.

177
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,800
He's even gotten
into the perfect position.

178
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,040
At a pitch nobody can hear,

179
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,520
I've been warming up my voice for ages.

180
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,440
I thought my phone was vibrating.

181
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:33,920
I was like...

182
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:37,120
He keeps revving
a motorcycle in his throat.

183
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:40,500
(Well, in that case...)

184
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,160
Teng, you're not on oxygen.

185
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,720
Don't pass out on us.

186
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,280
Quick, hook me up to the oxygen.

187
00:07:58,380 --> 00:07:59,900
(Teng's little helper)

188
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:02,520
When I sing today,

189
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,880
I might not sound nasal.

190
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:04,760
Your nose is stuffed?

191
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:07,100
(Not enough resonance)

192
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,040
It's too strong.

193
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,520
People will think
I'm getting my teeth cleaned.

194
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:21,380
(A sudden windstorm hits his face)

195
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:25,920
It pushed my contacts

196
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:26,880
right up under my eyelids.

197
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:27,920
Okay.

198
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,720
I've turned it on for you.

199
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:30,440
Getting any oxygen now?

200
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:31,800
Yeah, that's perfect.

201
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,960
Let's move the table.

202
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,760
Never wears them when he needs to.

203
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,040
So pale.

204
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:46,300
(Cover up. That's indecent)

205
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,480
Bai always dresses for the wrong season.

206
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,880
Is that what fashion is?

207
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:51,400
Are you wearing long johns?

208
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,240
The other day, when it was boiling hot,

209
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,240
he had long johns on.

210
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,160
With leather pants over them.

211
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,040
And a leather hat.

212
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:03,360
Hello, everyone.

213
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,200
(Chen Rui)
Here in the highlands,

214
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,760
there's an amazing butterfly.

215
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,600
It's called
the bright-banded satyr butterfly.

216
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,840
(Bright-banded satyr butterfly)
Do you know how many times

217
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,680
(A satyrine butterfly in the genus Lethe.)
a butterfly blinks per minute?

218
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:15,960
(Footage sourced online)
It actually never blinks.

219
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,120
In the butterfly world,

220
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,400
their vision works

221
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,640
nothing like ours.

222
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:21,480
Humans see like high-res cameras.

223
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,600
But a butterfly

224
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,880
only sees what's right in front of it.

225
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:26,040
(Bai Jingting)
So, for this challenge,

226
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:28,040
while you're singing,

227
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,520
(Fan Chengcheng)
you'll imitate butterflies and never blink.

228
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:31,920
Let's see who lasts the longest.

229
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:33,040
Alright, thanks, everyone.

230
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,880
(Singing Without Blinking)
Rules for singing without blinking.

231
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,600
The nine players split into two teams.

232
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,880
Each team sends one player

233
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,400
to challenge someone
from the other team.

234
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:45,680
Whoever blinks while singing is out.

235
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:48,280
The winner picks another opponent

236
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,360
and keeps taking on challengers

237
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,880
until the song ends.

238
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,920
The team with fewer player swaps wins.

239
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,800
So once the song's over,

240
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,960
the game's over too, right?

241
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,040
Yep.

242
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,240
Let's split into two.

243
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,080
Depends which team Lin Yi picks.

244
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,980
(A line divides them)

245
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,400
Wait, I get that much power?

246
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,680
I'll go with Teng, then.

247
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:09,200
Okay.

248
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,340
(The teams)

249
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,360
Time to prove myself.

250
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,060
(We're rooting for you)

251
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:14,040
(Showing off his talent)

252
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,200
I even got contacts

253
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,720
that are 0.5 diopters stronger in each eye.

254
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:19,640
The ones with the highest water content.

255
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:21,560
Nice.

256
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:24,140
(A worthy rival)

257
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,960
This won't be easy to win.

258
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:28,600
We've all got big eyes.

259
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:40,700
(Oh boy)

260
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,240
Come on.

261
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:48,380
(The veteran's back in action)

262
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,380
(Oh, I'm so scared)

263
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,320
You...

264
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,120
I'll take it. I'll go.

265
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:54,780
Here comes the gold standard.

266
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:56,260
(The poster girl for big eyes steps up)

267
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,600
Who's singing first on your team?

268
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,240
He's already grabbed the mic.

269
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:05,820
(Those dreamy eyes are ready for battle)

270
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,280
He's so competitive.

271
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,640
I really can't compete with him.

272
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,280
You're going first?

273
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:10,920
I am.

274
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:12,960
Actually, Anyu doesn't

275
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,320
have much of an advantage here.

276
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:16,320
He gets really emotional when he sings.

277
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,560
I tend to get carried away and go...

278
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:19,280
♪Nights when I miss you♪

279
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,620
(Can't help being sexy)

280
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:21,400
Exactly.

