♪These soft and tender thoughts of you♪

564
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:42,240
Something... I love you.

565
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:45,000
You two might as well return the mics.

566
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:47,700
(Nobody's singing anyway)

567
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,980
(The bouncing trick returns)

568
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:53,760
Soft...

569
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,360
I can barely watch.

570
00:23:58,080 --> 00:23:59,680
My eyes are watering again.

571
00:24:00,980 --> 00:24:01,900
(Jia Bing out)

572
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,180
(Song ends)
Four to one.

573
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:05,620
(Round two: Team Teng wins)
Team Teng wins.

574
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:06,200
I've got

575
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,880
really sensitive eyes.

576
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:08,600
You know?

577
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,000
How's he so good?

578
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,800
I didn't wanna blink and miss your gaze,

579
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:13,800
so I practiced at home.

580
00:24:13,820 --> 00:24:14,520
(Preparation pays off)
Oh my God.

581
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:15,480
Lin Yi.

582
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:16,520
He's incredible.

583
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:19,780
(Once missed Teng's gaze)

584
00:24:19,780 --> 00:24:21,980
(After intense training,
I swear I'll become)

585
00:24:21,980 --> 00:24:23,560
(The king of staring contests)

586
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:25,160
Why were you two holding each other

587
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:25,840
back there?

588
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:29,560
Just needed something to lean on.

589
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:31,280
They couldn't really control themselves

590
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:31,920
by then.

591
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,040
You didn't even know
what you were doing, huh?

592
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:37,280
Please, sit down.

593
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:38,280
No.

594
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:38,880
Teng.

595
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:40,040
Teng, have a seat.

596
00:24:41,040 --> 00:24:42,640
How does he manage not to blink?

597
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:43,480
That guy...

598
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:44,160
It's terrifying.

599
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:44,680
I can't do it either.

600
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:46,120
Not even close.

601
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:47,320
Even I can't do that.

602
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:48,700
(That sounded a little odd)

603
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:50,000
Then that's his problem.

604
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:53,120
I give up.

605
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:53,840
I'm seriously impressed.

606
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,520
After that quick warm-up,

607
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:30,120
it's time for today's main challenge.

608
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:31,120
Improv Music Video.

609
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:32,520
(Improv Music Video)
Pair up.

610
00:25:32,520 --> 00:25:34,160
Choose a song

611
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,480
from the show's playlist and improvise.

612
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,280
During the verses,

613
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:39,240
act out a scene together.

614
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,440
When the chorus starts,

615
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:42,280
switch straight into singing.

616
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:43,560
When the next verse starts,

617
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:45,000
go back to acting.

618
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:45,960
Keep switching

619
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:47,320
until the song ends

620
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:48,800
and finish telling your story.

621
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:52,640
These songs
would be great as DJ remixes.

622
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:54,360
Then suddenly switch to the remix.

623
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:57,840
♪Set me free♪

624
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:59,540
(That's the chemistry
of sitting side by side)

625
00:26:02,360 --> 00:26:03,660
Our group should...

626
00:26:03,660 --> 00:26:04,560
(A bunch who love acting and singing)

627
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:06,320
Be pretty good at this.

628
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:08,320
Lin Yi might be a little shy.

629
00:26:08,340 --> 00:26:09,440
(Still in his shy newbie phase)

630
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:11,280
But the rest of them

631
00:26:11,380 --> 00:26:13,500
(Absolute legends)
are real pros.

632
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,880
Go ahead
and pick your songs and partners.

633
00:26:17,980 --> 00:26:21,100
(Song list)

634
00:26:21,320 --> 00:26:23,000
What's I Want Freedom?

635
00:26:23,240 --> 00:26:25,400
(Starts singing instantly)
♪Maybe only you♪

636
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:28,120
(Lost in the music)
♪That's why you couldn't walk away♪

637
00:26:29,300 --> 00:26:30,780
(Why'd you get him started?)

638
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,440
♪Crying as you♪

639
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:38,340
(Huh?)

640
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:44,640
Find another partner.

641
00:26:44,700 --> 00:26:46,340
(Too shy for this)

642
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:48,120
Anyone have a favorite song?

643
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:48,960
You can pick first.

644
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,120
Let's start with Decent.

645
00:26:50,520 --> 00:26:51,400
Decent?

646
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:53,360
Gotta find someone decent, then.

647
00:26:54,060 --> 00:26:55,700
(I know what you mean)

648
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:56,920
Churan, don't pick me.

649
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:57,960
I don't really know that song.

650
00:26:59,550 --> 00:27:01,160
The second she said "someone decent",

651
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:02,400
Anyu's knee practically jerked.

652
00:27:03,900 --> 00:27:05,900
(Decency is a reflex)

653
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,920
She said she wanted someone decent.

654
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:13,360
You almost stood up, huh?

655
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:14,380
(Confidence is his thing)

656
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,160
I pick Lin Yi.

657
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:18,560
Lin Yi.

658
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:19,320
That was sudden.

659
00:27:20,080 --> 00:27:21,840
You're not decent enough.

660
00:27:22,800 --> 00:27:24,000
I might not sing it very decently.

661
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:28,080
Not sing it decently?

662
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:29,560
(There's no spare oxygen for all that laughing)
Not very decently?

663
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:30,960
It's fine. Just go for it.

664
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:31,800
Okay.

665
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:32,840
(Decent)

666
00:27:32,840 --> 00:27:34,000
Alright.

667
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:35,880
We'll play the song for you first.

668
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:38,480
You two can think about your scene

669
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,200
and get into character.

670
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:42,920
That hurts.

671
00:27:43,580 --> 00:27:44,520
(Already in character)

672
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:46,000
♪Don't pile up♪

673
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:49,200
You just want to sing.

674
00:27:50,300 --> 00:27:50,840
(No prep, straight into singing)

675
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:56,480
♪Don't pile on memories
and turn our story into a soap opera♪

676
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:59,140
(Who gave him the mic?)

677
00:28:00,340 --> 00:28:01,660
(Secretly stashed a mic for himself)
You've got another one!

678
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:07,520
♪After years of love,
why ruin something so beautiful?♪

679
00:28:11,120 --> 00:28:13,040
So decent.

680
00:28:14,880 --> 00:28:19,640
♪We're adults now,
with nothing owed between us♪

681
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:25,720
♪I willingly gave you my time♪

682
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:29,400
♪Like an actor after the final curtain♪

683
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:31,680
Isn't this supposed to be their song?

684
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:32,360
While we're singing,

685
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:33,240
you two should be acting.

686
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:33,800
It's just a demo.

687
00:28:33,800 --> 00:28:34,640
You do your thing.

688
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,200
He just wants to sing.

689
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,960
Hurry up and act.

690
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:41,740
(You'll miss your chance)

691
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:42,840
We're arguing.

692
00:28:43,520 --> 00:28:45,640
We're a couple trying
to break up gracefully.

693
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:46,640
You agreed to keep it civil,

694
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:48,280
but you keep dragging up

695
00:28:48,280 --> 00:28:50,160
(A natural-born screenwriter)
every little thing from your past.

696
00:28:50,500 --> 00:28:52,220
(What a storyteller)

697
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:54,840
Mr. Huang, let's act one out first.

698
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:55,720
No.

699
00:28:56,600 --> 00:28:57,840
Mr. Huang.

700
00:28:58,800 --> 00:28:59,640
No.

701
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:01,240
Come on, let's argue.

702
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:01,880
Let's fight.

703
00:29:02,780 --> 00:29:05,500
(Lip care time
for the stylish guy over 40)

704
00:29:09,380 --> 00:29:10,940
(Gets emotional in one second)

705
00:29:10,980 --> 00:29:12,780
(Switching to argument mode)

706
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:15,000
This song's actually great for acting.

707
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:15,760
No way.

708
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:18,240
Arguing to this song would really hurt.

709
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:18,640
Yeah.

710
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:20,240
(Easy to get emotional)
You'd get so sad arguing to this song.

711
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:22,000
Then when the chorus hits,

712
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:22,680
you snap out of it.

713
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,280
Don't glare at me later.

714
00:29:28,040 --> 00:29:29,800
What, should I argue nicely?

715
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:30,660
(Confused but cute)
A gentle argument?

716
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:31,880
You can blink this time.

717
00:29:32,660 --> 00:29:34,300
(Don't worry, I'll blink)

718
00:29:34,320 --> 00:29:35,080
Lin Yi's...

719
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,720
What's there to say?

720
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:41,880
Alright, ready.

721
00:29:50,420 --> 00:29:51,860
(Decent, Lin Yi and Wang Churan)

722
00:29:51,860 --> 00:29:54,180
(Scene: A couple arguing
on the verge of breaking up)

723
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:07,000
We've come to this.

724
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:09,840
Don't you think you're partly to blame?

725
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:11,800
I know what I did wrong.

726
00:30:12,360 --> 00:30:13,880
I know I can't sing.

727
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:15,640
But you didn't have

728
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:17,360
to embarrass me

729
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:18,480
in front of everyone.

730
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:19,280
I know I sing off-key,

731
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:20,720
but you could've harmonized with me,

732
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:22,120
right?

733
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:26,280
But how am I supposed
to harmonize with your rapping?

734
00:30:26,280 --> 00:30:27,240
Enough.

735
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:28,800
I've had enough.

736
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:29,560
I can practice.

737
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:31,560
I'd do anything for you.

738
00:30:36,080 --> 00:30:38,200
No, acting
to this song could make me cry.

739
00:30:41,560 --> 00:30:42,600
But I've fallen for someone else.

740
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:44,040
He sings way better than you.

741
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:55,640
What song did he win you over with?

742
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:02,880
He won me over

743
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,320
with Conquer.

744
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:06,520
Because he actually sings.

745
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:07,280
But you...

746
00:31:09,680 --> 00:31:10,880
You rap.

747
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:16,680
So you don't like rappers?

748
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:20,280
I like singers,

749
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:21,840
just not rappers.

750
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,760
What's so wrong with rap?

751
00:31:28,620 --> 00:31:31,720
♪We should part with dignity♪

752
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:35,300
♪Neither of us needs to apologize♪

753
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:37,010
♪We owe each other nothing♪

754
00:31:37,010 --> 00:31:40,760
♪I gave my heart,
knowing it could break♪

755
00:31:40,760 --> 00:31:42,560
♪Before the camera♪

756
00:31:42,560 --> 00:31:45,020
♪Are the people we once were♪

757
00:31:45,020 --> 00:31:46,060
(A foot-powered seat upgrade)

758
00:31:46,220 --> 00:31:47,020
(The forgotten comfort buddy)

759
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:52,300
♪The people we once were♪

760
00:31:52,300 --> 00:31:53,600
♪Cheering us on♪

761
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:57,230
♪Crying and screaming our hearts out♪

762
00:31:57,800 --> 00:32:00,970
♪Even goodbye should be graceful♪

763
00:32:00,970 --> 00:32:04,680
♪So all these years weren't wasted♪

764
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:06,570
♪We loved so fiercely♪

765
00:32:06,710 --> 00:32:10,780
♪And gave it everything we had♪

766
00:32:10,990 --> 00:32:12,600
♪Don't let obsession♪

767
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:15,420
♪Ruin our memories♪

768
00:32:15,420 --> 00:32:17,200
♪I loved you♪

769
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:20,510
♪Plain and simple♪

770
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:22,880
What was that singing?

771
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:24,800
You haven't improved
at all in all these years!

772
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:25,680
I've had enough.

773
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:27,560
Isn't my love enough for you?

774
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:39,920
Actually,

775
00:32:41,480 --> 00:32:42,640
you've improved quite a lot.

776
00:32:44,280 --> 00:32:45,240
There's something I've kept secret

777
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:46,240
from you all these years.

778
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:55,520
Actually,

779
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,880
I've been pretending to sing badly.

780
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:00,440
I'm actually a singer.

781
00:33:06,680 --> 00:33:09,810
♪Even goodbye should be graceful♪

782
00:33:09,810 --> 00:33:13,570
♪So all these years weren't wasted♪

783
00:33:13,730 --> 00:33:15,380
♪We loved so fiercely♪

784
00:33:15,510 --> 00:33:19,380
♪And gave it everything we had♪

785
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:21,330
♪Don't let obsession♪

786
00:33:21,330 --> 00:33:23,730
♪Ruin our memories♪

787
00:33:29,520 --> 00:33:31,120
♪I loved you♪

788
00:33:31,120 --> 00:33:34,080
♪Plain and simple♪

789
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:41,640
From now on,
every penny I earn from my albums

790
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:42,840
will go straight to you.

791
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:47,280
Will you take me back?

792
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:52,040
Well, I guess I could consider it.

793
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,440
♪Goodbye♪

794
00:33:56,940 --> 00:34:03,840
♪I'm glad we met♪

795
00:34:07,060 --> 00:34:08,780
(Impressed)

796
00:34:08,780 --> 00:34:10,150
Oh my God.

797
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:13,240
Brilliant. Seriously brilliant.

798
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:14,080
That was great singing.

799
00:34:15,160 --> 00:34:16,160
Lin Yi's so adorable.

800
00:34:16,160 --> 00:34:16,800
It's like...

801
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:17,960
(Who invented this adorable Lin Yi?)

802
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:19,320
His soul and body
are two different people.

803
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:20,880
I laughed so hard I couldn't breathe.

804
00:34:21,660 --> 00:34:23,200
(Confused but cute)

805
00:34:23,200 --> 00:34:23,480
No.

806
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:25,560
It's how seriously Lin Yi
takes it that's hilarious.

807
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:28,480
There was even that part

808
00:34:28,480 --> 00:34:30,920
where you told her, "I'm actually a singer."

809
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:32,800
♪Yesterday♪

810
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:34,040
That's actually true.

811
00:34:35,660 --> 00:34:36,940
(Seriously?)

812
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:38,360
On all the major music platforms,

813
00:34:38,360 --> 00:34:39,800
I'm actually listed as a singer.

814
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:46,000
I've released songs.

815
00:34:46,620 --> 00:34:47,540
(It's true)

816
00:34:47,580 --> 00:34:49,180
(The jokes just keep coming)

817
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:50,640
Those two are hilarious.

818
00:34:53,600 --> 00:34:55,280
I feel like they've
totally outshined us.

819
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:56,360
How do we even follow that?

820
00:34:56,920 --> 00:34:58,600
(Leave it to the pros)
You two can go next.

821
00:34:58,600 --> 00:34:59,160
Come on.

822
00:34:59,160 --> 00:35:00,120
Let's go next.

823
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:01,240
Sure.

824
00:35:01,240 --> 00:35:02,120
What's our storyline?

825
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:03,360
Let's just argue.

826
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:04,760
Whatever.

827
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:08,280
We're doing I Want Freedom.

828
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:09,040
Play it first.

829
00:35:14,760 --> 00:35:16,000
Whose version is this?

830
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:17,960
Mine, obviously.

831
00:35:17,980 --> 00:35:19,540
(Why did I even ask?)

832
00:35:21,280 --> 00:35:22,680
♪Everyone♪

833
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:25,780
(Song: I Want Freedom,
performed by Wang Anyu)

834
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,640
Just sit back and listen.

835
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,600
Lin Yi, I really did release this song.

836
00:35:31,620 --> 00:35:33,340
(He's that talented?)

837
00:35:35,280 --> 00:35:36,960
Then I won't ruin your song.

838
00:35:38,840 --> 00:35:40,600
Go ahead and yell at me all you want.

839
00:35:41,040 --> 00:35:42,240
Let's reenact yesterday's fight.

840
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:43,280
Sure, let's go.

841
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,800
Which fight yesterday?

842
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:47,400
The one where you mistook
Chengcheng for your teammate.

843
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:47,880
Oh man.

844
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:48,720
This wilderness.

845
00:35:48,720 --> 00:35:49,640
(The episode with Dumb
and Dumber's Guide to Werewolf)

846
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:50,520
Let me see.

847
00:35:51,340 --> 00:35:53,260
(Don't fight over me)

848
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:55,200
I thought you meant

849
00:35:55,200 --> 00:35:56,960
the fight we had
after filming yesterday.

850
00:35:56,980 --> 00:35:58,460
(Oh, we're doing this?)

851
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:00,720
You mean reenacting

852
00:36:00,720 --> 00:36:01,600
our chat messages?

853
00:36:03,760 --> 00:36:04,880
Alright, get ready.

854
00:36:13,100 --> 00:36:14,060
(I Want Freedom,
Bai Jingting and Wang Anyu)

855
00:36:14,060 --> 00:36:14,780
(Scene:)

856
00:36:14,780 --> 00:36:16,020
(Two best friends turn
against each other over Werewolf)

857
00:36:16,020 --> 00:36:16,720
(And get into a fight)

858
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:18,640
First, learn
to recognize your teammates.

859
00:36:18,640 --> 00:36:20,000
Didn't you think it was me?

860
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:22,040
Was it you?

861
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:23,400
Are you my boss?

862
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:29,800
Listen, Wang Anyu.

863
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:32,080
Playing Werewolf with you

864
00:36:32,080 --> 00:36:33,680
is just like
playing basketball with you.

865
00:36:33,680 --> 00:36:35,080
You never even see me!

866
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:41,560
I'm a pro at basketball and Werewolf.

867
00:36:41,560 --> 00:36:42,560
Who are you to criticize me?

868
00:36:42,560 --> 00:36:43,480
Think about last time.

869
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:44,200
What did I do?

870
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:47,000
I fought those huge guys for rebounds

871
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,160
just to pass you the ball.

872
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:49,640
And I

873
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:50,720
kept yelling, "Anyu!"

874
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:52,080
Anyu!

875
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:54,000
Just tell me, did we score?

876
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:54,960
Did we?

877
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:56,080
Didn't that shot go in?

878
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:57,080
I don't wanna hear it!

879
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,600
And what about yesterday?

880
00:37:03,080 --> 00:37:04,600
How many hints did I give you?

881
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:05,480
Why didn't you stand up first?

882
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:06,360
Why were you hugging him?

883
00:37:07,520 --> 00:37:09,600
Why'd you wait for Chengcheng

884
00:37:09,600 --> 00:37:10,760
to stand up before you did?

885
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:16,440
As

886
00:37:16,440 --> 00:37:17,880
a killer with a bullet,

887
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:19,880
I had to hide my identity.

888
00:37:20,480 --> 00:37:22,000
Is everything my fault?

889
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:24,080
Whose fault would it be? Mine?

890
00:37:25,980 --> 00:37:27,580
(Fine, it's all my fault)

891
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:30,880
After hearing that,

892
00:37:30,880 --> 00:37:33,320
what was our friendship all these years?

893
00:37:34,550 --> 00:37:37,280
♪Maybe only you♪

894
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,520
♪Understand me♪

895
00:37:38,520 --> 00:37:41,920
♪That's why you couldn't walk away♪

896
00:37:42,410 --> 00:37:44,320
♪Crying as you♪

897
00:37:44,320 --> 00:37:45,850
♪Hold me close♪

898
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:47,000
They've even got choreography.

899
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:48,050
♪Whispering♪

900
00:37:48,050 --> 00:37:50,290
♪How much you love me♪

901
00:37:50,290 --> 00:37:51,690
♪Only you♪

902
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,440
♪Understand me♪

903
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:56,640
♪Like a trapped beast♪

904
00:37:57,120 --> 00:37:58,110
♪Inside a skyscraper♪

905
00:37:58,120 --> 00:37:59,000
They're so in sync!

906
00:37:59,160 --> 00:38:03,240
♪Longing for freedom♪

907
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:04,800
So what?

908
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:07,560
Was all that battling for nothing?

909
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:09,640
Those guys were even bigger than him.

910
00:38:10,180 --> 00:38:11,860
(What about my scene?)

911
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:13,440
Didn't I fight for rebounds?

912
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:15,440
Didn't I give my all under the basket?

913
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:17,400
I even brought you basketball shoes.

914
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:21,560
Didn't I wash them for you afterward?

915
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:25,280
Did you even get them clean?

916
00:38:27,240 --> 00:38:29,320
I wanted my scent to stay with you.

917
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:29,840
What's wrong with that?

918
00:38:30,240 --> 00:38:31,560
So whenever you see those shoes,

919
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:33,000
you'll think of me. Isn't that nice?

920
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:36,920
Your scent?

921
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:39,200
I know.

922
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:40,480
But it's fine.

923
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:41,360
Next time we play,

924
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:43,680
I'll invite you again.

925
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:44,640
Really?

926
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:46,320
Hengdian

927
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:48,680
will be our home court.

928
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:51,400
Nobody in Hengdian can beat us.

929
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,160
Exactly.

930
00:38:56,760 --> 00:38:59,870
♪Just give up this moment♪

931
00:38:59,870 --> 00:39:02,420
♪Maybe only you♪

932
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:03,920
♪Understand me♪

933
00:39:03,920 --> 00:39:07,470
♪That's why you couldn't walk away♪

934
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:09,700
♪Crying as you♪

935
00:39:09,700 --> 00:39:11,510
♪Hold me close♪

936
00:39:11,510 --> 00:39:13,470
♪Whispering♪

937
00:39:13,470 --> 00:39:16,150
♪How much you love me♪

938
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:20,610
♪Only you♪

939
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:22,230
♪Understand me♪

940
00:39:22,230 --> 00:39:25,590
♪Like a trapped beast♪

941
00:39:26,020 --> 00:39:27,970
♪Inside a skyscraper♪

942
00:39:27,970 --> 00:39:31,920
♪Longing for freedom♪

943
00:39:33,020 --> 00:39:35,370
♪Maybe only you♪

944
00:39:36,200 --> 00:39:37,180
♪Understand me♪

945
00:39:37,410 --> 00:39:40,450
♪That's why you couldn't walk away♪

946
00:39:40,820 --> 00:39:42,640
♪Crying as you♪

947
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:44,550
♪Hold me close♪

948
00:39:44,550 --> 00:39:46,360
♪Whispering♪

949
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:48,760
♪How much you love me♪

950
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:50,600
♪Only you♪

951
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:51,770
♪Understand me♪

952
00:39:51,770 --> 00:39:55,260
♪Like a trapped beast♪

953
00:39:55,710 --> 00:39:57,480
♪Inside a skyscraper♪

954
00:39:57,480 --> 00:40:01,120
♪Longing for freedom♪

955
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:09,280
Nasal resonance.

956
00:40:09,300 --> 00:40:11,180
(Waiting for a high five)

957
00:40:13,020 --> 00:40:13,540
(Never mind)

958
00:40:13,540 --> 00:40:15,560
He can recover
from that missed high five himself.

959
00:40:25,040 --> 00:40:26,480
I don't know about anyone else,

960
00:40:26,480 --> 00:40:27,640
but I admit defeat.

961
00:40:30,320 --> 00:40:31,960
Like the rest of us haven't already.

962
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:34,320
A 9.5 rating on social media.

963
00:40:34,380 --> 00:40:36,540
(12 out of 10 satisfied)

964
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:38,800
At least a 9.6.

965
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:40,600
That was fun.

966
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:42,600
Was it really?

967
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:44,360
It's kind of embarrassing, but...

968
00:40:45,100 --> 00:40:47,020
(Worth remembering)
It was fun.

969
00:40:47,040 --> 00:40:48,280
Is it really that embarrassing?

970
00:40:48,300 --> 00:40:50,300
(You looked like you were loving it)

971
00:40:54,460 --> 00:40:56,660
♪Maybe only you♪

972
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:02,880
It's like we've got dirt

973
00:41:02,880 --> 00:41:05,040
on each other now.

974
00:41:07,060 --> 00:41:09,140
(The embarrassment's sinking in)

975
00:41:09,160 --> 00:41:10,360
After a performance like that,

976
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:12,320
nobody else dares to go up.

977
00:41:12,320 --> 00:41:13,320
Mr. Huang, you're up!

978
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:15,280
What other songs are there?

979
00:41:16,140 --> 00:41:18,000
(Picking one he knows)

980
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:18,800
Annie works.

981
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:19,420
(Annie)

982
00:41:19,800 --> 00:41:21,000
You go, Teng.

983
00:41:21,760 --> 00:41:22,480
I actually know this one.

984
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:22,800
Exactly.

985
00:41:22,800 --> 00:41:24,320
Weren't you singing it earlier?

986
00:41:29,400 --> 00:41:30,440
Back in action.

987
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:34,360
We'd better stay out of this one.

988
00:41:34,460 --> 00:41:35,500
(Learning to live
without his comfort buddy)

989
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:36,440
I can already imagine

990
00:41:36,440 --> 00:41:38,000
all the new memes online.

991
00:41:38,340 --> 00:41:41,220
(Teng GIFs 2.0: Going to work,
waiting to leave, off work)

992
00:41:41,260 --> 00:41:42,360
(Here's another one)

993
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:43,840
(Hehehe)
How about we do a story

994
00:41:43,840 --> 00:41:45,760
where two brothers love the same girl?

995
00:41:45,760 --> 00:41:47,280
Two brothers fall for the same...

996
00:41:48,120 --> 00:41:49,760
It's so hard to argue with Teng.

997
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,520
You called me.
I've been waiting here forever.

998
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:55,320
Go on, Mr. Huang.

999
00:41:59,900 --> 00:42:01,180
(Scene: Two brothers fall
in love with Annie)

1000
00:42:01,180 --> 00:42:02,460
(The younger brother gives her up)

1001
00:42:02,460 --> 00:42:03,580
(Years later, the brothers reunite)

1002
00:42:07,440 --> 00:42:08,000
Teng.

1003
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:09,260
(Older brother, Jingyu)

1004
00:42:10,180 --> 00:42:12,140
(Younger brother, Teng)

1005
00:42:17,620 --> 00:42:18,940
(I don't usually laugh)

1006
00:42:18,940 --> 00:42:21,220
(Unless someone does this)

1007
00:42:25,920 --> 00:42:27,000
Strap an oxygen tank on me too.

1008
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:27,940
(Laughing so hard he can't breathe)

1009
00:42:29,920 --> 00:42:31,000
He looks so funny.

1010
00:42:32,640 --> 00:42:34,680
We came all the way up here to find her.

1011
00:42:34,680 --> 00:42:35,580
(Plot hole fixed)

1012
00:42:37,060 --> 00:42:40,180
(Annie, Huang Jingyu and Shen Teng)

1013
00:42:45,200 --> 00:42:46,520
I'm here, Teng.

1014
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:51,520
Where's Annie?

1015
00:42:53,720 --> 00:42:54,720
I don't know.

1016
00:42:56,880 --> 00:42:57,960
You don't know?

1017
00:42:59,760 --> 00:43:00,480
Don't lie to me!

1018
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:02,560
Where's Annie?

1019
00:43:05,200 --> 00:43:06,560
What did you promise me back then?

1020
00:43:19,840 --> 00:43:20,760
Teng,

1021
00:43:22,080 --> 00:43:23,280
you've pushed me down three times.

1022
00:43:24,120 --> 00:43:24,880
Stop pushing me.

1023
00:43:25,440 --> 00:43:26,120
I can't climb back up.

1024
00:43:28,920 --> 00:43:30,120
But Annie

1025
00:43:30,120 --> 00:43:31,240
will never be yours.

1026
00:43:35,940 --> 00:43:38,250
♪Annie♪

1027
00:43:38,800 --> 00:43:41,570
♪I can't lose you♪

1028
00:43:42,290 --> 00:43:44,530
♪Annie♪

1029
00:43:45,320 --> 00:43:48,400
♪I can't forget you♪

1030
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:51,260
♪Annie♪

1031
00:43:51,680 --> 00:43:55,000
♪I call out to you with all my heart♪

1032
00:43:56,520 --> 00:44:01,040
♪I'll love you forever♪

1033
00:44:02,180 --> 00:44:03,180
(Laughing actually hurts now)

1034
00:44:03,200 --> 00:44:05,400
Their timing right
before the chorus is perfect.

1035
00:44:07,800 --> 00:44:08,200
Jingyu,

1036
00:44:10,520 --> 00:44:12,360
if I'd known what kind of man you were,

1037
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:14,720
I never would've

1038
00:44:14,720 --> 00:44:15,960
given up my true love for you.

1039
00:44:17,760 --> 00:44:18,520
Back then,

1040
00:44:18,520 --> 00:44:19,760
it was never our choice.

1041
00:44:21,600 --> 00:44:23,040
It was Annie's choice.

1042
00:44:26,160 --> 00:44:26,920
You're wrong.

1043
00:44:27,440 --> 00:44:28,800
You're so naive.

1044
00:44:30,480 --> 00:44:31,760
I was the one who told her

1045
00:44:34,080 --> 00:44:35,080
to go with you.

1046
00:44:41,200 --> 00:44:43,240
I'm sorry for all these years.

1047
00:44:44,920 --> 00:44:48,720
I never imagined...

1048
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:50,920
You let her down,

1049
00:44:50,920 --> 00:44:52,560
but you let me down even more.

1050
00:44:54,240 --> 00:44:55,600
Well, if I've let you both down,

1051
00:44:57,080 --> 00:44:58,240
at least let us be happy.

1052
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:01,720
Where is she?

1053
00:45:04,240 --> 00:45:05,640
When she heard we were meeting,

1054
00:45:06,440 --> 00:45:07,400
she left.

1055
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:09,360
Then should we...

1056
00:45:10,960 --> 00:45:12,360
Go find her together?

1057
00:45:14,670 --> 00:45:17,120
♪Annie♪

1058
00:45:17,920 --> 00:45:21,020
♪I can't lose you♪

1059
00:45:21,310 --> 00:45:23,660
♪Annie♪

1060
00:45:24,360 --> 00:45:27,240
♪I can't forget you♪

1061
00:45:27,840 --> 00:45:30,350
♪Annie♪

1062
00:45:30,660 --> 00:45:34,000
♪I call out to you with all my heart♪

1063
00:45:35,270 --> 00:45:39,780
♪I'll love you forever♪

1064
00:45:45,080 --> 00:45:46,000
Take care of yourself.

1065
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:01,120
Annie,

1066
00:46:02,400 --> 00:46:03,320
he's gone.

1067
00:46:12,120 --> 00:46:13,560
You little punk!

1068
00:46:25,040 --> 00:46:26,320
What a veteran performer.

1069
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:29,440
Come on, you two are up.

1070
00:46:29,440 --> 00:46:31,040
Chengcheng and I will do Silence.

1071
00:46:31,590 --> 00:46:37,050
♪I can't help becoming a stubborn fish♪

1072
00:46:38,580 --> 00:46:43,030
♪Swimming alone against the current♪

1073
00:46:44,640 --> 00:46:46,480
But now that it's over...

1074
00:46:46,480 --> 00:46:47,920
I was just gonna say.

1075
00:46:47,920 --> 00:46:49,200
They really got carried away.

1076
00:46:52,000 --> 00:46:53,520
We're all people with some dignity.

1077
00:46:53,780 --> 00:46:55,260
(That wasn't really us earlier)

1078
00:46:56,680 --> 00:46:58,680
I think you should stab me.

1079
00:46:58,780 --> 00:47:01,080
(Plot discussion underway)
I'll lie down up front.

1080
00:47:01,080 --> 00:47:01,720
But

1081
00:47:01,720 --> 00:47:03,760
we should still have that

1082
00:47:03,760 --> 00:47:04,840
if there's another life,

1083
00:47:04,840 --> 00:47:05,680
we'll fight again moment.

1084
00:47:05,680 --> 00:47:06,360
Something like that.

1085
00:47:06,880 --> 00:47:07,920
Let's take it one step at a time.

1086
00:47:10,520 --> 00:47:11,480
Let's go.

1087
00:47:17,820 --> 00:47:18,540
(Silence, Hu Xianxu and Fan Chengcheng)

1088
00:47:18,540 --> 00:47:19,100
(Scene:)

1089
00:47:19,100 --> 00:47:20,060
(Bitter rivals
who secretly respect each other)

1090
00:47:20,060 --> 00:47:20,940
(Lifelong rivals,
always trying to outdo each other)

1091
00:47:30,760 --> 00:47:32,000
Do you know what time it is?

1092
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:33,400
Why'd you drag me out here so late?

1093
00:47:36,720 --> 00:47:39,480
You used to be my greatest rival

1094
00:47:40,160 --> 00:47:42,160
and the person I respected most.

1095
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:43,520
What happened to you?

1096
00:47:44,200 --> 00:47:44,800
What'd I do?

1097
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:49,440
You're the only person in this world

1098
00:47:49,440 --> 00:47:50,800
I've ever found

1099
00:47:51,320 --> 00:47:52,600
worth defeating.

1100
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:56,160
We've faced off seven times.

1101
00:47:56,160 --> 00:47:57,800
You lost all seven.
What more do you want?

1102
00:48:01,640 --> 00:48:03,240
Is that so hard to accept?

1103
00:48:06,960 --> 00:48:09,840
Rock, paper, scissors!

1104
00:48:13,240 --> 00:48:14,720
Not bad, kid.

1105
00:48:14,720 --> 00:48:16,480
You've been practicing behind my back.

1106
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:18,680
Of course the eighth time is different.

1107
00:48:19,880 --> 00:48:22,440
The eighth time really is different.

1108
00:48:23,840 --> 00:48:24,400
Chengcheng,

1109
00:48:26,560 --> 00:48:27,520
is there something

1110
00:48:28,040 --> 00:48:29,280
you haven't told me?

1111
00:48:31,080 --> 00:48:31,880
I'll come clean.

1112
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:35,840
I came here to tell you something.

1113
00:48:35,840 --> 00:48:36,440
Go ahead.

1114
00:48:37,360 --> 00:48:38,600
From our seven battles,

1115
00:48:38,600 --> 00:48:40,120
I've learned

1116
00:48:40,120 --> 00:48:40,600
so much.

1117
00:48:42,200 --> 00:48:43,720
But today, I'm here to tell you...

1118
00:48:44,840 --> 00:48:45,920
I'm terminally ill.

1119
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:52,680
Buddy,

1120
00:48:53,360 --> 00:48:55,080
what illness do you have?

1121
00:48:55,360 --> 00:48:57,120
Why couldn't you tell me?

1122
00:48:58,320 --> 00:48:59,800
I'm crazy.

1123
00:49:03,200 --> 00:49:04,320
You're crazy?

1124
00:49:05,200 --> 00:49:06,000
Why?

1125
00:49:06,880 --> 00:49:10,040
Why didn't you tell me, Chengcheng?

1126
00:49:10,040 --> 00:49:12,320
Before I go, I want

1127
00:49:12,920 --> 00:49:14,000
to see you one last time

1128
00:49:14,960 --> 00:49:16,040
and play one final game of...

1129
00:49:17,560 --> 00:49:21,240
rock, paper, scissors.

1130
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:25,480
Buddy,

1131
00:49:26,520 --> 00:49:27,880
this is our final showdown.

1132
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:30,280
Let's give it everything we've got

1133
00:49:30,920 --> 00:49:32,640
in one last round

1134
00:49:32,640 --> 00:49:35,560
of rock, paper, scissors.

1135
00:49:37,780 --> 00:49:42,490
♪Love sentenced me
to a lifetime of loneliness♪

1136
00:49:43,370 --> 00:49:46,190
♪I won't fight back♪

1137
00:49:46,840 --> 00:49:49,440
♪I won't let go♪

1138
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:54,310
♪An endless circle
I can't finish drawing♪

1139
00:49:54,820 --> 00:49:57,640
♪A love that can never fill my heart♪

1140
00:49:57,960 --> 00:50:00,800
♪It's you♪

1141
00:50:02,120 --> 00:50:05,560
Rock, paper, scissors!

1142
00:50:05,580 --> 00:50:10,320
♪Why does love
condemn us all to loneliness?♪

1143
00:50:10,840 --> 00:50:13,720
♪I can't break free♪

1144
00:50:14,290 --> 00:50:17,130
♪I can't escape♪

1145
00:50:18,980 --> 00:50:21,840
♪The worries I can't untangle♪

1146
00:50:22,280 --> 00:50:25,200
♪The fate I can't escape♪

1147
00:50:25,390 --> 00:50:28,570
♪It's you♪

1148
00:50:46,280 --> 00:50:47,200
I'm glad I met you.

1149
00:50:52,600 --> 00:50:53,920
(Rehabilitation center)
Chengcheng in bed six,

1150
00:50:53,920 --> 00:50:54,880
you're cleared for discharge.

1151
00:51:09,240 --> 00:51:10,200
That was really deep.

1152
00:51:11,440 --> 00:51:11,960
You know?

1153
00:51:11,960 --> 00:51:12,640
This guy's

1154
00:51:12,640 --> 00:51:13,960
been mentally ill for years,

1155
00:51:14,800 --> 00:51:15,800
and they're such good friends.

1156
00:51:15,800 --> 00:51:16,560
He doesn't even realize it.

1157
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:18,680
So you see?

1158
00:51:18,680 --> 00:51:19,600
You're a patient too.

1159
00:51:20,800 --> 00:51:21,880
This is brilliant.

1160
00:51:21,880 --> 00:51:22,840
It could be a comedy sketch.

1161
00:51:24,840 --> 00:51:26,360
Neither of them is normal.

1162
00:51:26,360 --> 00:51:28,120
They both think it's a terminal illness.

1163
00:51:29,360 --> 00:51:30,440
For my next music video,

1164
00:51:30,440 --> 00:51:31,240
I'll just use this footage

1165
00:51:31,240 --> 00:51:32,480
and put my song over it.

1166
00:51:32,480 --> 00:51:32,960
Keep it real.

1167
00:51:32,960 --> 00:51:34,040
Let's keep it real.

1168
00:51:35,240 --> 00:51:36,440
Karaoke's over.

1169
00:51:36,440 --> 00:51:38,120
Now, we've got

1170
00:51:38,120 --> 00:51:40,360
a little challenge involving darkness.

1171
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:44,680
♪Set me free♪

1172
00:51:44,680 --> 00:51:46,880
♪From this mysterious wait♪

1173
00:52:29,480 --> 00:52:30,200
Come on.

1174
00:52:30,200 --> 00:52:30,920
Let's go.

1175
00:52:31,760 --> 00:52:33,640
Are we supposed
to lie down on the floor?

1176
00:52:35,400 --> 00:52:36,160
Sit on the floor.

1177
00:52:37,740 --> 00:52:38,960
(Sitting in a row)

1178
00:52:38,960 --> 00:52:40,720
Can we see how dark it gets?

1179
00:52:41,060 --> 00:52:41,820
(Lights out)

1180
00:52:41,860 --> 00:52:44,300
(Night vision mode)
Ah!

1181
00:52:44,340 --> 00:52:45,980
(What was that noise?)

1182
00:52:46,020 --> 00:52:46,760
(I'm sweet and innocent)

1183
00:52:46,760 --> 00:52:47,640
This is exciting.

1184
00:52:47,640 --> 00:52:48,600
(I'm sweet and innocent)
So exciting.

1185
00:52:48,600 --> 00:52:49,200
(I'm cold and ruthless)

1186
00:52:49,200 --> 00:52:51,080
Should you take off your necklaces?

1187
00:52:55,040 --> 00:52:56,320
Your shirt's so see-through.

1188
00:52:57,080 --> 00:52:58,000
Seriously?

1189
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:00,480
We even get a bonus show.

1190
00:53:01,400 --> 00:53:01,880
You're putting it back on?

1191
00:53:01,880 --> 00:53:02,680
This...

1192
00:53:06,120 --> 00:53:07,920
Can I wear your jacket?

1193
00:53:07,920 --> 00:53:08,320
Is that okay?

1194
00:53:08,320 --> 00:53:08,880
Sure.

1195
00:53:09,560 --> 00:53:10,600
I'm way too hot.

1196
00:53:11,520 --> 00:53:14,320
Our next game
is called Eat Bananas in the Dark.

1197
00:53:15,200 --> 00:53:17,160
(Eat Bananas in the Dark)
Players can only move

1198
00:53:17,160 --> 00:53:18,280
when the lights are off.

1199
00:53:18,280 --> 00:53:19,480
When the lights come on,

1200
00:53:19,480 --> 00:53:22,320
everyone must freeze immediately.

1201
00:53:22,320 --> 00:53:25,160
(Starting point)
Anyone caught moving goes back to the start.

1202
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:27,320
(Bananas)
Bananas will drop randomly around the room.

1203
00:53:27,320 --> 00:53:27,960
Once you've eaten one,

1204
00:53:27,960 --> 00:53:30,040
you can attack with its peel

1205
00:53:30,040 --> 00:53:31,360
to eliminate other players.

1206
00:53:31,360 --> 00:53:33,440
(One peel can eliminate only one player)
Last one standing wins.

1207
00:53:33,440 --> 00:53:36,720
We'll also randomly drop

1208
00:53:36,720 --> 00:53:38,480
a Taobao Magic Magnifier each round.

1209
00:53:38,960 --> 00:53:41,160
(Magnifier)
Whoever finds it must hold it up

1210
00:53:41,160 --> 00:53:42,600
and shout, "Expand my view!"

1211
00:53:43,080 --> 00:53:45,160
The lights will come on
for three seconds.

1212
00:53:45,520 --> 00:53:47,360
Everyone must stop moving.

1213
00:53:47,360 --> 00:53:49,480
It can only be used once per round.

1214
00:53:49,480 --> 00:53:50,560
After the game,

1215
00:53:50,560 --> 00:53:52,720
you'll also receive a Tmall
11.11 Global Shopping Festival

1216
00:53:52,720 --> 00:53:54,360
Tech Gift Box.

1217
00:53:55,760 --> 00:53:57,360
Once everyone's
back at the starting line...

1218
00:53:58,800 --> 00:53:59,360
How do we play?

1219
00:53:59,840 --> 00:54:02,120
Let's try it and see how dark it gets.

1220
00:54:03,560 --> 00:54:04,600
Three.

1221
00:54:04,600 --> 00:54:05,640
(Practice round)
Two.

1222
00:54:05,640 --> 00:54:06,200
One.

1223
00:54:06,340 --> 00:54:07,300
(Lights out)

1224
00:54:07,300 --> 00:54:09,820
(Night vision mode: Bai Jingting,
Wang Anyu, Wang Churan, Lin Yi)

1225
00:54:09,860 --> 00:54:11,540
(Fan Chengcheng, Jia Bing)

1226
00:54:13,100 --> 00:54:17,060
(Banana is free)

1227
00:54:22,220 --> 00:54:23,460
(Empty)

1228
00:54:23,480 --> 00:54:24,840
When did you throw that?

1229
00:54:25,720 --> 00:54:26,780
I'll finish eating, then get her.

1230
00:54:26,780 --> 00:54:28,260
(Night vision mode: Wang Anyu)

1231
00:54:28,460 --> 00:54:29,940
(Got a banana)

1232
00:54:29,980 --> 00:54:31,380
(Quick getaway)

1233
00:54:36,600 --> 00:54:37,560
Who's got a banana?

1234
00:54:37,580 --> 00:54:39,940
(Bananas in hand: Hu Xianxu, Wang Anyu)

1235
00:54:41,260 --> 00:54:42,980
(Night vision mode)

1236
00:54:42,980 --> 00:54:44,580
(Looking for a target)

1237
00:54:46,180 --> 00:54:47,780
(Found the magnifier)

1238
00:54:48,280 --> 00:54:48,800
Expand!

1239
00:54:50,380 --> 00:54:51,360
(Find the magnifier
and shout "Expand my view!")

1240
00:54:51,360 --> 00:54:52,240
Watch out.

1241
00:54:52,240 --> 00:54:53,220
(Lights come on for three seconds)

1242
00:54:54,660 --> 00:54:55,520
(Wang Anyu and Hu Xianxu
finish their bananas)

1243
00:54:55,520 --> 00:54:57,440
(Banana peels can now be used to attack)
Anyu and Hu now have banana peels.

1244
00:54:57,440 --> 00:54:59,040
They can attack
other players when it's dark.

1245
00:54:59,360 --> 00:55:00,280
This is dangerous.

1246
00:55:00,280 --> 00:55:01,080
Banana peels.

1247
00:55:01,540 --> 00:55:02,680
(Ready to attack when lights go out:
Wang Anyu, Hu Xianxu)

1248
00:55:02,680 --> 00:55:04,120
Bye, Bai. See you.

1249
00:55:04,280 --> 00:55:05,320
Let's form an alliance.

1250
00:55:05,320 --> 00:55:05,840
